  designNotes: "2026-09-02, Meshy AI attack (\u6ED1\u884C\u7FFB\u6EFE.zip / sliding_rool,
    take \"Scene\", 2.77s, from the \u5C41\u5B69\u738B Man-in-Black rig - retargets
    fine). A rolling pounce: nt 0-0.70 the boss rolls low along the ground (hipY
    drops to 0.18, feet over the top nt 0.65), then rises nt 0.72-0.80 into a downward
    blade sweep (blade speed peak 42 at nt 0.80, bladeY 3.9 -> 1.0) - that exit slash
    is the hit (window nt 0.74-0.90). Hips forward-drift 0 -> ~20m baked into the
    body pose (worst of the batch) -> cancelClipBodyDrift=1 anchors the visible body;
    lungeDistanceFromTargetGap (gap-1m, clamp 0..9) carries the boss forward toward
    the player over the roll window nt 0-0.68, so from the ~3.5m standoff it rolls
    ~2.5m and from 8m it rolls ~7m - a real gap-closer. Wired as attack per user
    choice (b) \"\u7FFB\u6EFE\u64B2\u64CA roll + hit\" (not (a) an evasion). deflectReaction
    ContinueCombo, knockback 0 per session rules. NEEDS PLAY TUNING: the roll reads
    OK with the body anchored + FSM-carried? lungeTargetGapMeters, hit window nt,
    whether a light contact hit during the roll itself (nt 0.15-0.35) is wanted."
